// Z80 bus ownership — the declared context.
//
// The 68k can only read/write Z80 RAM, or drive a blocking VDP copy, while it
// OWNS the Z80 bus. `with z80_stopped { … }` is the door for EVERY 68k hold in
// the tree (since LS-13b, 2026-09-17 — before that, all but one): the bracket splices the request-and-spin before its body and the release
// after it, and the compiler PROVES the pairing — every path through the body
// reaches the release (`[context.escape]`), no branch enters the region past
// the request (`[context.entry-skip]`), and the hold is never taken twice
// (`[context.reacquire]`, because a bus request is not a counting lock: an
// inner release frees the outer hold).
//
// THE SLOT. `z80_stopped(interleave: Code = asm {})` — a context parameter
// (sigil's named slot, owner decision d-33, sigil 2ff47f97/c64edab4). The acquire
// is `request ++ interleave ++ grant spin`, so a consumer may place code BETWEEN
// the bus request and the spin, and nowhere else. Omitted, it is `asm {}` and
// appends nothing: the 22 bare brackets emitted byte-identical ROMs across the
// canonical landing shapes when it was added (LS-13b, measured by whole-ROM
// comparison, s4 / s4.debug / demo.debug). The slot is spliced INSIDE the
// acquire range, so all three proofs above cover it; slot code is authored to the
// CONSUMER's proc for the clobber/SR lints. Limits a slot author meets at once:
// the `++` chain in a context field must stay on one line; a label inside an
// `asm { }` value is not reachable from the body; and a FALSE comptime gate on
// the bracket (`with z80_stopped(…) if COND`) removes the slot along with the
// acquire.
//
// COLD BOOT WAS THE ONE EXCEPTION UNTIL LS-13b. `EntryPoint` in
// engine/system/boot.emp used to spell its own request/spin/release by hand
// (`move.w d7,(a1)` / `.wait_z80` / `move.w d0,(a1)`, with a1 preloaded from
// BootData), because releasing Z80 reset (`move.w d7,(a2)`) has to happen between
// the bus request and the grant spin. That one statement is now the slot
// argument — `with z80_stopped(interleave: asm { move.w d7, (a2) }) { … }` — so
// boot's hold carries the same compiler proofs as every other, and its
// request/release are the absolute `#$0100`/`#$0000` writes sigil's `[bus.*]`
// tier recognises (the register-indirect spelling was invisible to it). The a1
// preload was deleted with it. Do NOT hand-spell a hold again: the census gate
// refuses any code outside this module that names Z80_BUS_REQUEST.
//
// ---- THE CENSUS OF 68k Z80-BUS HOLDS ----------------------------------------
// STOP READING THE PROSE AND RUN THE GATE. Since LS-13a (2026-09-07) this census
// is DERIVED on every build, not maintained by hand:
//
//     python3 tools/test_z80_bus_hold_mask_census.py
//
// prints today's population, every site's masking mechanism, and the tally. It is
// collected by build.sh's pre-build pytest lane and is build-fatal. The paragraphs
// below explain what it checks and why; the NUMBERS in them are a snapshot
// (2026-09-07, re-taken 2026-09-17 for LS-13b) and the tool is the authority when
// they disagree.
//
// TOTAL: 23, ALL bracketed (was 22 bracketed + 1 hand-spelled until LS-13b). By
// file: sound_api 6 · vblank 6 · section 3 · bg 2 · boot 2 · controllers 1 ·
// parallax 1 · sound_debug 1 · ojz_scroll_test 1.
//
// METHOD, so it can be re-run and so it can fail. Two greps, both QUOTED (an
// unquoted `--include=*.emp` is eaten by this workspace's zsh and matches
// NOTHING while exiting 1), both with this file as the positive control:
//   1. `grep -rn "with z80_stopped" --include='*.emp' --include='*.asm' engine games`
//      → the CODE sites are the hits that are not prose (`grep -E ':[0-9]+: *//'`):
//      22 through LS-13a, 23 since LS-13b. Only the CODE count is a durable
//      number — the hit and prose counts are partly a function of THIS HEADER, so
//      they move whenever it is edited, and they did, inside the parcel that
//      wrote them (LS-13a corrected 27/5 to 28/6 here).
//   2. The search that catches a hold which BYPASSES the bracket is now a gate,
//      not a grep: `test_no_hand_spelled_bus_hold_remains` in the census tool
//      fails if any CODE line (comments and strings stripped) outside this module
//      names `Z80_BUS_REQUEST` or `$A11100`, other than the constant's one
//      definition in engine/system/constants.emp. A hold has to write that
//      register and code can only reach it by name or address, so a
//      hand-spelled request, a preload of the address into a register, or a
//      second context all fail it. HISTORY, because the grep this replaced was
//      wrong in an instructive way: until LS-13b boot's hand-spelled hold wrote
//      through a1 (`move.w d7,(a1)` / `move.w d0,(a1)`), so a grep for the NAME
//      found only a comment in boot.emp, and the real route was
//      `dc.l Z80_BUS_REQUEST` in BootData's movem preload — exactly the line the
//      gate would now refuse. Sigil's `[bus.*]` net had the same blind spot
//      (sigil-frontend-emp/src/z80_bus.rs: a register-indirect destination is
//      unresolvable, its soundness bailout, and the source was not the literal
//      `#$0100` either).
//
// SITES ARE NAMED BY ROUTINE, NOT BY LINE, DELIBERATELY. A line-numbered census
// is stale the first time anyone edits one of these files — this one went stale
// inside its own parcel, from its own edits.
//
// EVERY ONE OF THE 23 IS ENTERED WITH INTERRUPTS MASKED, by one of four
// mechanisms — which is why no comment anywhere may call itself "the one hold
// that must also stay masked". The gate recognises all four FROM CODE (it strips
// string literals and `//` comments before matching, so no comment — including
// this one — can satisfy it), and the tally it printed on 2026-09-17 (LS-13b) was
// `{'HAND_2700': 7, 'INTS_OFF': 6, 'RESET_SR': 2, 'VBLANK': 8}` (on 2026-09-07,
// RESET_SR 1 plus boot's then hand-spelled hold, which the scanner could not see):
//   * INTS_OFF (6) — enclosing `with ints_off`: Sound_PostByte, Sound_ReadStat
//     and Sound_PlayMusic's two (its `.await_slot` probe and its param-block
//     post), Parallax_Update's reg $0B reassert, the OJZ scroll test;
//   * HAND_2700 (7) — a hand-spelled `move.w #$2700, sr` in force from earlier in
//     the same proc: Sound_Init's `.wait_alive` probe, Sound_DrainSfxRing,
//     BG_Init's two blits, Section_RedrawPlanes' three. BG_Init and
//     Section_RedrawPlanes set their mask hundreds of lines above the brackets it
//     covers, and BOTH carry a DEBUG `IPL >= 6` assert rather than resting on the
//     reader's trust. (docs/DEFERRED_WORK.md's LS-13 row says ×5 for this class
//     and totals 21 — that is an arithmetic slip, corrected there;
//     Section_RedrawPlanes contributes three, not one.)
//   * VBLANK (8) — the 68000's own IPL 6 on IRQ entry: VInt_Level's three,
//     VInt_Lag's three, Read_Controllers, Sound_DebugMirror. ⚠ THIS CLASS IS NOT
//     "an argument", and the LS-13 write-up filed it as one. All eight procs
//     declare `requires(vblank)`, which sigil PROVES at every call site
//     (`[context.unsatisfied]`, engine/irq.emp) against a capability whose sole
//     `grants(vblank)` root is VBlank_Handler — so unreachability from the main
//     loop is machine-checked, not reasoned. Sound_DebugMirror was the ONE site
//     that lacked the clause; it declares it since LS-13a, and the gate asserts
//     the single-grant-root premise the whole class rests on. What is NOT proven
//     for this class is that the handler never LOWERS the mask before the
//     bracket; the gate checks that too, per-proc, by refusing any `sr` write
//     ahead of the site.
//   * RESET_SR (2) — the reset SR ($2700) still standing. EntryPoint's Z80 init
//     bracket (the one carrying the `interleave` slot) and its YM key-off
//     bracket; boot's FIRST `sr` write is after both of them, and the gate checks
//     that ORDERING (test_reset_entry_holds_precede_the_first_sr_write) rather
//     than trusting it — and that the slot-carrying bracket is still there, so a
//     regression to a hand-spelled boot hold fails loudly.
// The mask matters because the hold is a LATCH: an IRQ6 whose handler takes its
// own bracket RELEASES the bus on the way out, and nothing below a `.wait_z80`
// re-issues the request.
//
// WHAT IS STILL UNPROVEN, so the next reader does not over-read the gate:
//   * ~~PAIRING for boot's hand-spelled hold~~ — CLOSED by LS-13b (2026-09-17).
//     Boot's hold is a bracket; an early `jbra` out of its body was measured
//     REFUSED by `[context.escape]` (the same mutation on the old hand spelling
//     built green). Sigil's `[bus.*]` tier also now SEES it: a stray
//     `move.w #$0000, Z80_BUS_REQUEST` inside the body reports
//     `[bus.start-without-stop]` in EntryPoint (0 on the old spelling). Note that
//     tier is REPORT-ONLY (`sigil build --native --report contracts`), not
//     build-fatal, and nothing in sigil checks that a declared bus context is
//     recognised as one (sigil c64edab4's booked gap).
//   * INTERPROCEDURAL MASK LOWERING. The gate is per-proc: a `jbsr` between a
//     HAND_2700 mask and its bracket could lower the mask inside the callee
//     unseen. It DERIVES and prints the count of sites in that shape on every run
//     (1 on 2026-09-07: Section_RedrawPlanes' last bracket, past its
//     `jbsr Section_GetSecPtrXY`; 2 on 2026-09-17: that one and BG_Init's second
//     blit — not re-investigated by LS-13b, which did not touch either).
//   * A build-time check of the mask AT THE HOLD, in the compiler rather than in
//     a text gate. Not expressible in `.emp` today: sigil models bus state
//     (z80_bus.rs's `Tri` net over `must_in_states`) but has NO interrupt-mask
//     lattice, so `z80_stopped` cannot declare "requires masked". The framework
//     for one already exists — see docs/DEFERRED_WORK.md, LS-13a.
// `tools/test_sound_bus_hold_mask_lint.py` remains as sound_api's file-scoped
// twin; it additionally checks that file's header still STATES the rule.
//
// SHAPE-GATED SITES, so "in the sound build" claims can be checked rather than
// asserted: `SOUND_DRIVER_ENABLED == 0` gates VInt_Level's and VInt_Lag's OFF
// fences and Section_RedrawPlanes' middle bracket; `== 1` gates the flag-bracket
// raise/lower pairs in all three of those routines; Sound_DebugMirror is zero
// bytes in BOTH canonical shapes (triple gate, see its header). Everything else
// is unconditional — including `Read_Controllers`, which is why vblank.emp's
// old "the ONLY 68k bus hold in the sound build" was false.
//
// Consumers `use engine.z80_bus.{z80_stopped}`.
//
// The acquire/release are spelled INLINE rather than calling a template: a
// context's halves evaluate in the CONSUMER's scope, so a cross-module context
// may only name link-resolved symbols. `Z80_BUS_REQUEST` is exactly that — a
// bare link-resolved hardware address (truth: engine/system/constants.emp)
// each splice site resolves through the link.
//
// Pure comptime module: opens no section and emits ZERO bytes anywhere in the
// ROM — bytes appear only where a consumer brackets with it.
module engine.z80_bus

pub context z80_stopped(interleave: Code = asm {}) {
    // Request the bus, run the consumer's `interleave` slot (empty by default —
    // `asm {}` appends nothing, so a bare `with z80_stopped` emits exactly the
    // stream it emitted before the parameter existed), then spin until the Z80
    // grants it. The slot is spliced INSIDE the acquire, so every bracket proof
    // covers it (sigil d-33; see the header's "THE SLOT" paragraph).
    // The `++` chain must stay on ONE line: a context field's expression ends at
    // the line end, and newlines are legal only inside the `asm { }` braces.
    acquire = asm { move.w  #$0100, Z80_BUS_REQUEST } ++ interleave ++ asm {
    .wait_z80:
        btst    #0, Z80_BUS_REQUEST
        bne     .wait_z80
    }
    // Release it.
    release = asm {
        move.w  #$0000, Z80_BUS_REQUEST
    }
}
